<header><p class="st-kicker">margraviate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Brandenburg-Ansbach</h1><p class="st-meta">1398 CE – 1791 CE · capital Ansbach</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hohenzollern margraviate around Ansbach in Franconia, an early Lutheran state that was sold to Prussia by its last margrave in 1791.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The 1398 division of the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/burgraviate-of-nuremberg">Burgraviate of Nuremberg</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-elector-of-brandenburg">Frederick VI</a>, later the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollern</a> elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, the territory 'below the mountains' around Ansbach. From the 15th century it was usually ruled by a younger Hohenzollern son as margrave.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-iii-achilles-elector-of-brandenburg">Albert Achilles</a>, who also became elector, made Ansbach a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollern</a> power, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-the-pious">George the Pious</a> introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in 1528. The principality was rich in farmland and governed through a strong bureaucracy. Ansbach's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> residence was built in the 18th century, and the margraves hired out soldiers to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American War of Independence</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The last margrave, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-alexander-margrave-of-brandenburg-ansbach">Charles Alexander</a>, inherited the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-brandenburg-bayreuth">Principality of Brandenburg-Bayreuth</a> in 1769 and in 1791 handed both principalities to his Prussian cousins before retiring to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> ceded Ansbach to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria">Kingdom of Bavaria</a> in 1806.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-brandenburg-ansbach.jpg" alt="Principality of Brandenburg-Ansbach" width="320" height="224"><figcaption>Image: Mikmaq · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Principality_of_Ansbach_1791.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1398 CE – 1791 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>margraviate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ansbach</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Albert Achilles, George the Pious, Charles Alexander</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>East Franconian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Margraviate of Ansbach, Ansbach</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1594&amp;focus=principality-of-brandenburg-ansbach" aria-label="Principality of Brandenburg-Ansbach on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4924 459 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Brandenburg-Ansbach lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5244 715L5250 710M5244 715L5229 694M5244 715L5300 622M5244 715L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5250 710h0M5229 694h0M5300 622h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5244 715h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5244 715h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ansbach. <a href="/atlas?year=1594&amp;focus=principality-of-brandenburg-ansbach">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
